  "cover_text": "Residential buildings account for a significant amount of the national energy use, and yet only 15 percent of them consume less than 200 kilowatt hours of electricity per year. The Burlington Free Will Community Medical Center in Massachusetts makes this a top priority by requiring all staff members to install low-errancy devices across their office areas and building general lighting.\n“Without the use of these systems, our healthcare providers, our engineers, our technicians – the backbone of the insurance companies, the Nursing Homes, Children’s Programs – at least 615 hospitals, and about 1,400 nursing homes in the United States had to self-fund lighting.” Michael J. Friedenberg, Chief Vice President of Electrical Services and Interventions\nThere are important elements our billing experts and facility management personnel must consider, however, when helping lead your healthcare community in this endeavor.\nWe are talking about:\n- What are you looking for?\n- What materials are best for the job\n- What aspects of your solution",
